{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"pnpm add @tanstack/charts @angular/common @angular/core @angular/platform-browser","lang":"sh"},{"type":"code","value":"import { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/angular'\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\n@Component({\n  imports: [Chart],\n  template: `<tanstack-chart [options]=\"chartOptions\" />`,\n})\nexport class RevenueChart {\n  chartOptions = {\n    definition: defineChart(createRevenueChart(rows), { tooltip }),\n    ariaLabel: 'Revenue by month',\n    aspectRatio: 16 / 9,\n  }\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The single "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" input works with immutable values and signals. The\nstandalone component ships as a partial-compiled Angular package."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"lifecycle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Lifecycle"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ngOnChanges"},{"type":"text","value":" creates or updates one shared adapter controller.\nAngular's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"afterNextRender"},{"type":"text","value":" mounts it into the prerendered surface in the\nbrowser, and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ngOnDestroy"},{"type":"text","value":" cleans it up. Replace the complete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":" value\nwhen chart state changes; mutating the existing object does not produce an\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OnPush"},{"type":"text","value":" input change. Callbacks such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onFocusChange"},{"type":"text","value":" are functions inside\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":", not Angular outputs."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"browser-and-server-status","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Browser and server status"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The verified package contract covers complete SVG server rendering through\nAngular's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderApplication"},{"type":"text","value":", browser mount, immutable updates, and teardown.\nWith "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"provideClientHydration"},{"type":"text","value":", the adapter adopts the existing server-rendered\nSVG and mark nodes, preserves them through immutable updates, and cleans up\non destruction. Installed-package checks cover Angular 19 and 22 AOT builds\nin Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit, not every version within the peer range."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"presentation-and-rendering","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Presentation and rendering"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.class"},{"type":"text","value":" and the string "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.style"},{"type":"text","value":" apply to the inner\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".ts-chart-host"},{"type":"text","value":"; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options.className"},{"type":"text","value":" applies to the rendered chart surface.\nThe component starts with SVG and can compose marks that use\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"canvasChartRenderer"},{"type":"text","value":". Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"renderSvg"},{"type":"text","value":" to replace SVG serialization without\nreplacing the shared host."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exports: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartCommonOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartOptions"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPresentationOptions"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyDirective"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartTooltipBodyTemplateContext"},{"type":"text","value":",\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ChartPoint"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"tooltip-body-composition","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tooltip body composition"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Project an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ng-template"},{"type":"text","value":" with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"[tanstackChartTooltipBody]=\"chartOptions.definition\""},{"type":"text","value":" for Angular-owned\ncontent. The definition binding is the generic type witness for strict template\nchecking; it does not configure behavior a second time. Render\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tooltip.defaultBody"},{"type":"text","value":" through "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"NgTemplateOutlet"},{"type":"text","value":" to retain native rows and\nswatches. The shared host owns focus, placement, portaling, inert transient\nstate, pinning, and dismissal; Angular owns the embedded-view lifecycle."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the "},{"type":"link","href":"./reference/chart.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Chart"},{"type":"text","value":" reference"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"link","href":"../../reference/chart-definitions.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chart Definition API"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"lifecycle","text":"Lifecycle","level":2},{"id":"browser-and-server-status","text":"Browser and server status","level":2},{"id":"presentation-and-rendering","text":"Presentation and rendering","level":2},{"id":"tooltip-body-composition","text":"Tooltip body composition","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts @angular/common @angular/core @angular/platform-browser\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/angular'\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\n@Component({\n  imports: [Chart],\n  template: `<tanstack-chart [options]=\"chartOptions\" />`,\n})\nexport class RevenueChart {\n  chartOptions = {\n    definition: defineChart(createRevenueChart(rows), { tooltip }),\n    ariaLabel: 'Revenue by month',\n    aspectRatio: 16 / 9,\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe single `options` input works with immutable values and signals. The\nstandalone component ships as a partial-compiled Angular package.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\n`ngOnChanges` creates or updates one shared adapter controller.\nAngular's `afterNextRender` mounts it into the prerendered surface in the\nbrowser, and `ngOnDestroy` cleans it up. Replace the complete `options` value\nwhen chart state changes; mutating the existing object does not produce an\n`OnPush` input change. Callbacks such as `onFocusChange` are functions inside\n`options`, not Angular outputs.\n\n## Browser and server status\n\nThe verified package contract covers complete SVG server rendering through\nAngular's `renderApplication`, browser mount, immutable updates, and teardown.\nWith `provideClientHydration`, the adapter adopts the existing server-rendered\nSVG and mark nodes, preserves them through immutable updates, and cleans up\non destruction. Installed-package checks cover Angular 19 and 22 AOT builds\nin Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit, not every version within the peer range.\n\n## Presentation and rendering\n\n`options.class` and the string `options.style` apply to the inner\n`.ts-chart-host`; `options.className` applies to the rendered chart surface.\nThe component starts with SVG and can compose marks that use\n`canvasChartRenderer`. Use `renderSvg` to replace SVG serialization without\nreplacing the shared host.\n\nExports: `Chart`, `ChartCommonOptions`, `ChartOptions`,\n`ChartPresentationOptions`, `ChartTooltipBodyDirective`,\n`ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`, `ChartTooltipBodyTemplateContext`,\n`ChartDefinition`, and `ChartPoint`.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\nProject an `ng-template` with\n`[tanstackChartTooltipBody]=\"chartOptions.definition\"` for Angular-owned\ncontent. The definition binding is the generic type witness for strict template\nchecking; it does not configure behavior a second time. Render\n`tooltip.defaultBody` through `NgTemplateOutlet` to retain native rows and\nswatches. The shared host owns focus, placement, portaling, inert transient\nstate, pinning, and dismissal; Angular owns the embedded-view lifecycle.\n\nSee the [`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) and\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Angular Adapter\ndescription: Render TanStack Charts with an Angular standalone component.\n---\n\n```sh\npnpm add @tanstack/charts @angular/common @angular/core @angular/platform-browser\n```\n\n```ts\nimport { Component } from '@angular/core'\nimport { Chart } from '@tanstack/charts/angular'\nimport { defineChart } from '@tanstack/charts'\nimport { tooltip } from '@tanstack/charts/tooltip'\n\n@Component({\n  imports: [Chart],\n  template: `<tanstack-chart [options]=\"chartOptions\" />`,\n})\nexport class RevenueChart {\n  chartOptions = {\n    definition: defineChart(createRevenueChart(rows), { tooltip }),\n    ariaLabel: 'Revenue by month',\n    aspectRatio: 16 / 9,\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe single `options` input works with immutable values and signals. The\nstandalone component ships as a partial-compiled Angular package.\n\n## Lifecycle\n\n`ngOnChanges` creates or updates one shared adapter controller.\nAngular's `afterNextRender` mounts it into the prerendered surface in the\nbrowser, and `ngOnDestroy` cleans it up. Replace the complete `options` value\nwhen chart state changes; mutating the existing object does not produce an\n`OnPush` input change. Callbacks such as `onFocusChange` are functions inside\n`options`, not Angular outputs.\n\n## Browser and server status\n\nThe verified package contract covers complete SVG server rendering through\nAngular's `renderApplication`, browser mount, immutable updates, and teardown.\nWith `provideClientHydration`, the adapter adopts the existing server-rendered\nSVG and mark nodes, preserves them through immutable updates, and cleans up\non destruction. Installed-package checks cover Angular 19 and 22 AOT builds\nin Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit, not every version within the peer range.\n\n## Presentation and rendering\n\n`options.class` and the string `options.style` apply to the inner\n`.ts-chart-host`; `options.className` applies to the rendered chart surface.\nThe component starts with SVG and can compose marks that use\n`canvasChartRenderer`. Use `renderSvg` to replace SVG serialization without\nreplacing the shared host.\n\nExports: `Chart`, `ChartCommonOptions`, `ChartOptions`,\n`ChartPresentationOptions`, `ChartTooltipBodyDirective`,\n`ChartTooltipBodyRenderContext`, `ChartTooltipBodyTemplateContext`,\n`ChartDefinition`, and `ChartPoint`.\n\n## Tooltip body composition\n\nProject an `ng-template` with\n`[tanstackChartTooltipBody]=\"chartOptions.definition\"` for Angular-owned\ncontent. The definition binding is the generic type witness for strict template\nchecking; it does not configure behavior a second time. Render\n`tooltip.defaultBody` through `NgTemplateOutlet` to retain native rows and\nswatches. The shared host owns focus, placement, portaling, inert transient\nstate, pinning, and dismissal; Angular owns the embedded-view lifecycle.\n\nSee the [`Chart` reference](./reference/chart.md) and\n[Chart Definition API](../../reference/chart-definitions.md).\n"}
